<title>UK: Fannie Mae sets 1.0 bln stg June 2002 bond.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae sets 1.0 bln stg June 2002 bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following global bond was announced by joint lead managers BZW and Merrill Lynch International Ltd.</p>
<p> BORROWER   FEDERAL NATIONAL MORTGAGE ASSOCIATION</p>
<p> AMT    1.0 BLN STG   COUPON     **	  MATURITY    07.JUN.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    19.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.25	REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+10 BP</p>
<p> NOTES    **TO BE PRICED.</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1	   SALE LIMITS US/GB</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  U.S.	TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.10	SELL CONC  0.15	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 7.00 PCT GILT DUE 07.JUN.02  </p>
<p> NOTES	AT 1425 GMT, THE YIELD ON THE 7.00 PCT GILT DUE</p>
<p>		JUN.2002 YIELD WAS 6.82 PCT.</p>
<p>		7.00 PCT GILT DUE NOV.2001 WAS YIELDING 6.84 PCT.</p>
<p>		9.75 PCT GILT DUE AUG.2002 WAS YIELDING 6.96 PCT.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
